      title: "Non-linear propagation: where harmonics come from",
      objectives: ["u10-o2"],
      html: `<p class="lead">Compressions travel a touch faster than rarefactions, so the wave slowly warps — and a warped wave contains new frequencies.</p>
<p>Everything you learned earlier assumed sound behaves <i>linearly</i>: a pure sine wave in, the same pure sine wave (just smaller) out, travelling at one fixed speed of 1,540 m/s in soft tissue. That is a very good approximation for small pressures. It is not exactly true.</p>
<p>In the <b>compression</b> half of the cycle the tissue is squeezed, so it is momentarily <b>denser and stiffer</b>, and sound travels <b>slightly faster</b> there. In the <b>rarefaction</b> half the tissue is stretched and slightly <b>slower</b>. Picture a line of runners where everyone in the front half speeds up a bit and everyone in the back half slows down: the shape of the line distorts. Over several centimetres of travel, the once-symmetric sine wave develops a steep, shark-fin-like front edge.</p>
<p>A distorted wave is, mathematically, no longer a single frequency. It is the original fundamental <b>plus</b> energy at 2f<sub>0</sub>, 3f<sub>0</sub> and so on. This is <span class="kw">non-linear propagation</span>, and the harmonics it creates are <span class="kw">tissue harmonics</span>. They are not reflected from anything — they are <b>manufactured along the way</b> by the tissue the pulse is passing through.</p>
<p>Three consequences follow directly, and they explain everything in the next lesson:</p>
<ul>
<li>Harmonics need <b>distance</b> to build up, so there are essentially none at the transducer face.</li>
<li>Harmonics need <b>intensity</b>, so they form where the beam is strongest.</li>
<li>Harmonics are generated on the way <b>out</b>, from a beam that has already been shaped — the returning harmonic echo carries that cleaner shape.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout key">Non-linear propagation: compressions travel slightly faster than rarefactions → the waveform distorts with distance → new energy appears at 2× the fundamental.</div>
<div class="callout warn">Trap: tissue harmonics are <i>created</i> during propagation, not reflected by a special structure. Nothing in the body "sends back" a harmonic the way a mirror sends back light.</div>`,
